flowchart TB
    accTitle: Acknowledgment, provider readback, and partial recovery
    accDescr: The applying host reads current managed labels, records a verified no-op when the desired state already exists, and otherwise requests the required addition. A clear or ambiguous response is followed by provider observation before any retry or removal. Earlier verified work remains real when a later operation fails; the result is partial, not rolled back.

    read("Read current managed labels"):::focus
    noop("If the required label is already present: record a verified no-op"):::ok
    request("Otherwise request the required managed-label addition")
    observe("After a clear or ambiguous response: observe current labels before any retry or removal"):::focus
    stop("If the addition is not observed: stop; do not remove or claim success"):::bad
    remove("If the addition is observed: remove the obsolete managed label, then read back")
    success("If final readback matches: intended managed state verified"):::ok
    partial("If a later operation fails or source moves: preserve the verified addition and return partial or incomplete"):::bad

    read --> noop
    read --> request
    request --> observe
    observe --> stop
    observe --> remove
    remove --> success
    remove --> partial
